# QEMU runs its CPU on a worker thread and shares memory with it, which a
# browser only permits on a cross-origin isolated page. Scoped to this one
# route: isolation also means every cross-origin subresource must consent to
# being embedded, and there is no reason to impose that on pages that gain
# nothing from it.
#
# The fonts this site loads do consent — Google serves them with
# cross-origin-resource-policy: cross-origin — which is the only reason this is
# a header change rather than a font migration.
/krsz-vm
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/krsz-vm/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
